    &lt;script&gt;
        // Start Date: October 17, 2025, at 2:44 PM (14:44:00)
        const START_DATE = new Date(&quot;2025-10-17T14:44:00&quot;).getTime();

        const milestones = [
            {
                id: 1,
                title: &quot;Katy's Birthday&quot;,
                shortDesc: &quot;A rollercoaster of emotions for JJ&quot;,
                longDesc: &quot;My first fond memory of ‘us’ is when you invited me to your birthday party. It was honestly quite unexpected from my end, and I cannot put into words the excitement, joy and hope I felt when you invited me. When I got the invite, I’m pretty sure I texted my friends, and they were like ‘you’re kidding’. One of my friends even asked me if I asked to go to your birthday party instead of being invited haha. I think that’s how unbelievable it was, and that’s how big of a crush I had on you during that time. In all honesty, you and your friends made a genius move to allow me to bring a plus one because I think I would’ve been too nervous to attend! Your party was definitely a rollercoaster of emotions for me. That night, I thought that you either still liked Will, or you guys were dating, especially with him being able to grab that seat next to you. In that moment, I felt quite sad haha. The rest of the night went well, and we were able to ride our scooters together! (although we fell behind sooo much that kyle had to go back to check on us) I was honestly quite scared of you falling off if I tried driving so I let you ride your own scooter. And, because we valued our lives so much, we decided to teach you how to ride a scooter down the sketchiest alleyway ever. I also remember going to the casino, and then bar hopping around and then playing never have I ever, and kiss marry kill. My hopes rose again when you said out of the three, you’d go out on a date with me, but they were killed once again when you said you’d kiss me, and marry Will. I now understand you were trying not to be obvious, but I think that night you made me sad twice lol, and I was so confused on whether you liked me or not. I think I thought to myself like why won’t she marry me or date me? We then went to karaoke later that night, and when we had to leave, I got my first ever hug from you, and I think our relationship was all uphill from then on! I remember walking out the karaoke place, and calling albin and sooking and crying to him about everything. I also remember going home, getting locked out the house, and getting yelled at but at that moment i didnt care at all, and I went to go find soju to drink in the dark haha. Although that night was a rollercoaster, I think I sometimes look back and laugh at my thought process, and it is going to go down as one of my most memorable nights ever, if not my most memorable one. Maybe our children will hear this story.&quot;,
                quote: &quot;JJ did not sook about this the night he got home, or the days after ~ The ghost in JJ's room&quot;,
                icon: &quot;sparkles&quot;
            },
            {
                id: 2,
                title: &quot;Movie night&quot;,
                shortDesc: &quot;Mooncakes, Labubu's, a spinning mirror, and near car crash at Hungry Jacks&quot;,
                longDesc: &quot;This was our first ever ‘date’ or ‘hangout’ but hey, you can decide on what you wanted it to be. I remember asking my friends how to ask you to go, and being so nervous when i sent that message. Luckily, the pretty girl i asked to go to the cinemas with me said yes! I remember you getting lost in Elizabeth, and coming maybe 15 minutes late. Leading into the movie, I wasn’t sure on whether I was more scared and nervous to watch the movie, or whether I was more scared and nervous to be sitting next to the girl that I had a crush on! During the movie, there were many times where I wanted to hold your hand, but I wasn’t sure if that was our dynamic yet. I also remember you laughing at literally every scary scene, and thinking back, the signs were there. After the movie, I gave you a Labubu, and some mooncakes that were somewhat expensive for their size. I thought that was it after, and was initially planning to leave leave after that because I wasn’t sure what to do, but you initiated something related to driving me and I was more than up for it! I think driving us around, going to the hungry jacks drive through and nearly crashing, getting some ice creams, and then talking for a while was honestly really sweet, and I was another chance to get to know you. I remember you said in the car that you wanted me to stay longer, and I thought that was really sweet, and I think those were some of the hints that I desperately needed to know that you possibly liked me back! I remember when we were leaving, since some got lost on the way to Elizabeth, I decided to lead the way back to your house so that you wouldn’t get lost another time. (especially since it was dark already) I think that was the simpiest thing that I had done at the time, and I don’t regret it one bit. I also remember getting to your house and asking for a hug by saying ‘hug!’ and when I left, I was like, omg why’d I say it like that.&quot;,
                quote: &quot;A date or a hangout, we'll never know 👀&quot;,
                icon: &quot;sparkles&quot;
            },
            {
                id: 3,
                title: &quot;Oktoberfest&quot;,
                shortDesc: &quot;Katy on a committee as always, and a night to remember&quot;,
                longDesc: &quot;I remember Oktoberfest somewhat well, and I know that it was on a Friday right after clinic. I remember mid-year, when it was brought up I wasn’t gonna go, but as it got closer to the date, I decided to go because I honestly liked you even more. I remember buying a Banh Mi, and was going to give it to you at Clinic, but someone took the bus instead while I was at the shopping centre like 3 minutes away haha. I then drove to the city, and that honestly took way longer than expected because I got caught up in about 10 different traffic jams. I remember then finally meeting you at the uni, and accompanying you to where you were working and sitting on the floor for god knows how long haha. Buuut, before we did that, we did get to go on a nice little walk and I enjoyed it very much. I remember midway through your shift, I decided to go on a run because I was cold, and to maybe get rid of some of the nerves. I also remember SOMEONE being a bad influence and giving me some of their beer, and I also remember throwing grass at you because I was bored. After you finished your shift, we immediately left that somewhat dead festival, and went to chinatown! I remember getting those korean corndogs with you, where it took like half an hour for it to come out. However, those thirty minutes went by pretty fast with us both spilling our family tea/lore to each other, and I think that was the first time that I really learnt a lot about you and your family. This day was also the day I made you try my favourite big-back spot called meet desserts where they had that 1L Boba, I actually never ended up finishing that cup because I only got it as an excuse to spend sliiightly more time with you.&quot;,
                quote: &quot;First night in chinatown foreshadowing many more to come&quot;,
                icon: &quot;heart-handshake&quot;
            },
            {
                id: 4,
                title: &quot;17 October 2025&quot;,
                shortDesc: &quot;The day it all happened, the day JJ dreamt of every night&quot;,
                longDesc: &quot;I remember asking you if you knew who I liked on the train, and then you literally led me on to think that you thought that I liked someone else. I was so worried on the train, and when I got home. Anyways, let’s fast forward past that embarrassing time! I remember asking you what we were because my friends were asking. Obviously, we knew who we both liked at that point, and the feelings were mutual. Although I knew all this, I did not expect for you to ask me out as I was in clinic, and it was honestly sooo unexpected. I can’t lie, when I saw it, I had the biggest smile on my face, and walking out of clinic, my eyes were glued to my phone to shoot you back a reply as soon as I could. You really do know how to make me the happiest guy alive, before and after us starting our relationship. &lt;3&quot;,
                quote: &quot;Walked in clinic single, walked out clinic taken.&quot;,
                icon: &quot;compass&quot;
            }
        ];

        const memoryNotes = [
            { id: 1, category: &quot;Sweet Moment&quot;, title: &quot;Lunch Dates&quot;, desc: &quot;Our little lunch dates where we'd go eat something we crave.&quot;, tag: &quot;Thoughtful&quot;, icon: &quot;coffee&quot; },
            { id: 2, category: &quot;Inside Joke&quot;, title: &quot;Uncontrollable Laughs&quot;, desc: &quot;Our little laughs and gags&quot;, tag: &quot;Laughter&quot;, icon: &quot;smile&quot; },
            { id: 3, category: &quot;Comfort&quot;, title: &quot;Cozy Days &amp; Nights&quot;, desc: &quot;Staying inside, watching a shows or a movie, and enjoying each others company.&quot;, tag: &quot;Cozy&quot;, icon: &quot;cloud-rain&quot; },
            { id: 4, category: &quot;Adventure&quot;, title: &quot;Car Rides&quot;, desc: &quot;Driving around with you and the crazy Adelaide traffic&quot;, tag: &quot;Adventure&quot;, icon: &quot;car&quot; },
